.TH SDL_strlcat 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_strlcat \- Concatenate strings.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_strlcat(char *dst, const char *src, size_t maxlen);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function appends up to
.BR maxlen
-
.BR SDL_strlen (dst)
- 1 characters from
.BR src
to the end of the string in
.BR dst ,
then appends a null terminator\[char46]
.PP
.BR src
and
.BR dst
must not overlap\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR maxlen
-
.BR SDL_strlen (dst)
- 1 is less than or equal to 0, then
.BR dst
is unmodified\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I dst
The destination buffer already containing the first null-terminated string\[char46] Must not be NULL and must not overlap with
.BR src \[char46]

.TP
.I src
The second null-terminated string\[char46] Must not be NULL, and must not overlap with
.BR dst \[char46]

.TP
.I maxlen
The length (in characters) of the destination buffer\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the length (in characters, excluding the null terminator) of the string in
.BR dst
plus the length of
.BR src \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_strlcpy (3)
